# Testing & DX (agents)

## Prefer leaf tests over client smoke

| Change touches | Add/extend tests in |
|----------------|---------------------|
| NBT endian / compounds | `nbt.Tests` |
| LevelDB WAL/snapshot/API | `leveldb.Tests` |
| Frame reliability / split / indexes | `raknet.Tests` |
| World overlay, intents, config, palettes, packet DTOs | `zenith.Tests` |

`dotnet test zenith.sln` should stay green. Do not treat Bedrock client connect as a substitute for format/invariant tests.

## What to test next (priority if growing features)

1. **Intent contracts** — queue overflow, ChatSystem does not require receive-thread fan-out, BlockSystem drains FIFO.
2. **Critical packet round-trips** — encode→decode for Login/StartGame/UpdateBlock/Text/InventoryContent (Packets layer only).
3. **RakNet receive path** — reliable window dedup, fragment bounds (DoS caps), NACK retransmit uses locked send.

## DX do / don't

```text
✅ Smallest leaf first; InternalsVisibleTo for internal types
✅ Document trade-offs in docs/decisions.md when behavior changes
✅ Config via zenith.yml (AppContext.BaseDirectory) — no new ZENITH_* env soup
❌ New DI / plugin / Actor “to make testing easier”
❌ Silent InMemory fallback when LevelDB open fails
❌ Drive-by refactors unrelated to the task
```

Narrative DX: [`docs/dx.md`](docs/dx.md). Keep docs candid about non-goals.
